&Q000460

{1 = 1-8}
11.	Lady, going to the sweet-voiced cows and gentle-voiced calves in the cattle-pen, 
12.	young woman, when you arrive there, 
13.	@wDN{Inana}, may the churn sound! 
14.	May the churn of your spouse sound, 
15.	@wDN{Inana}, may the churn sound! 
16.	May the churn of @wDN{Dumuzid} sound, 
17.	@wDN{Inana}, 
18.	may the churn sound! 

{9 = 9-14}
99.	The rocking of the churn will sing (?) for you, 
910.	@wDN{Inana}, may it thus make you joyous! 
911.	The good shepherd, the man of sweet songs, 
912.	will loudly (?) sing songs for you; lady, 
913.	with all the sweetest things, @wDN{Inana}, 
914.	may he make your heart joyous! 

{15 = 15-20}
1515.	Lady, when you enter the cattle-pen, @wDN{Inana}, 
1516.	the cattle-pen will indeed rejoice over you. 
1517.	Mistress, when you enter the sheepfold, @wDN{Inana}, 
1518.	the sheepfold will indeed rejoice over you. 
1519.	When you enter the feeding-pen, 
1520.	healthy ewes will spread out their wool for you. 

{21 = 21-24}
2121.	May the holy sheepfold abundantly provide (?) you with butter, 
2122.	may the cattle-pen produce butter and cream for you! 
2123.	May abundance endure in the sheepfold, 
2124.	may the days of @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}} be numerous! 

{25 = 25-26}
2525.	May my spouse, a ewe cherishing its lamb, 
2526.	be praised with sweet admiration! 
